        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skoss:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/A8F1-NPV9</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Genomic data refers to the genome and DNA data of an organism. They are used in bioinformatics for collecting, storing and processing the genomes of living things. Genomic data is a more extensive term than sequencing data. However genomic data mostly come from sequencing techniques. It may include non-sequencing data such as data from microarrays, data from real-time PCR panels and data from pharmacogenomics studies. [Source: Adapted from https://www.techopedia.com/definition/31247/genomic-data]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
