        <IRI>http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/MW8G-3CR8</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">In order to obtain a patent, a software invention must not fall under other non-patentable subject matter (for example, abstract ideas or mathematical theories) and has to fulfill the other substantive patentability criteria (for example, novelty, inventive step [non-obviousness] and industrial applicability [usefulness]). [Source: https://www.wipo.int/patents/en/faq_patents.html]</Literal>
